    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`. The audit output confirms a well-formed value: `NSW` (region) + `26` (2-digit fiscal year) + `16E6609E` (upper-hex HASH8) + `3` (Luhn CHK over the digits of `NSW2616E6609E`).\n\nChanges made:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` schema properties with one `memberId` property (regenerates `OwnerDto` at build time). Updated the `locality` description to reference `memberId`.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Renamed the stored field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id`, with `getMemberId`/`setMemberId`.\n- **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Renamed `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id` and widened the VARCHAR to 32 to accommodate the longer id (and any `-<n>` de-dup suffix). Seed `data.sql` never populated the column, so no data changes were needed.\n- **`rest/controller/v1/MemberId.java`** (replaces `CustomerCode.java`) \u2014 Composes `region + FY2 + HASH8 + CHK`, where `HASH8` reuses the same SHA-256-over-(normalizedTelephone+lastName) first-8-upper-hex, and `CHK` is `LuhnCheckDigit` over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 `buildMemberId`/`deduplicateMemberId` now derive and de-duplicate the `memberId` (collision handling applies to `memberId`); the fiscal year feeds the FY segment; `primaryIdentifier`, the human audit line, and the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event (now `memberId` field) all reference the member id.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Dropped the `checkDigit`/`membershipNumber` mappings; `memberId` auto-maps from the entity; `locality`/`timezone` now derive from the member id.\n- **`mapper/OwnerLocality.java`** \u2014 Replaced `forCustomerCode` with `forMemberId`, extracting the region as the leading run of letters (the delimiter-less format's REGION segment).\n- **`mapper/OwnerSegment.java`** \u2014 Uses `forMemberId(owner.getMemberId())` for the owner-segment region.\n\nNote: the task states these are behavior changes (collision handling, fiscal-year value, audit record, and owner segment now key off `memberId`), which are all reflected above.",
